WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:02.540
There’s a tiny
hole in the window.

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:05.349
The tiny hole is in
the inner structural

00:00:05.389 --> 00:00:08.290
pane—the middle layer
in our illustration.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:10.973
And crucially, it
doesn’t go all the way

00:00:11.013 --> 00:00:13.510
through the window
assembly to the outside.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.202
The tiny opening
connects the cabin’s air

00:00:16.242 --> 00:00:18.442
pressure with that
space between the

00:00:18.482 --> 00:00:19.840
structural panes.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.582
The outer pane carries
the normal pressure

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.523
difference between
the cabin and

00:00:24.563 --> 00:00:25.870
the outside air.

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:27.630
That’s Why Is That?
